Don't substract the cart rule discount from the subtotal the reward points value is sized against
JIRA ticket: IPET-3760

The subtotal is built as price * qty - base_discount_amount, so any cart price rule shrinks it and the same points become worth less.
With the "500 Points = CHF 10" rule, 1000 points came out as 17.88 instead of 20.00 once percent50 was applied.
base_discount_amount also carries the reward discount from the previous totals collection, so the subtotal refers to its own result and lands on a different amount on each recalculation.
Restores what do-not-substract-discount-from-item-price.patch provided until IPET-3296 constrained it to <3.0.58.

diff --git a/src/Rewards/Helper/Balance/Spend.php b/src/Rewards/Helper/Balance/Spend.php
--- a/src/Rewards/Helper/Balance/Spend.php
+++ b/src/Rewards/Helper/Balance/Spend.php
@@ -301,7 +301,12 @@
                         $itemPrice = $item->getBasePriceInclTax();
                     }
                     $itemPrice += (float)$item->getWeeeTaxAppliedAmountInclTax();
-                    $itemPrice = $itemPrice * $item->getQty() - $item->getBaseDiscountAmount();
+                    // BEGIN PATCH
+                    // don't substract the discount, it shrinks the subtotal that sizes the points value
+
+                    // $itemPrice = $itemPrice * $item->getQty() - $item->getBaseDiscountAmount();
+                    $itemPrice = $itemPrice * $item->getQty();
+                    // END PATCH
                 } else {
                     $itemPrice = $item->getBasePrice() * $item->getQty() - $item->getBaseDiscountAmount();
                 }
